{"t_ms": 10533, "event": {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011ChSmhdenEoJpG9kAuat99", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The patch violates ADR-0580. That ADR says an advance is not a release cut, so changelog rotation must not run in the advance's scoped mode (`--skip-changelog`). The patch removes the `skip_changelog` guard, so every sweep now rotates the changelog, including an advance.\n\nThe test `scripts/tests/test_release_advance.sh` guards this rule. It runs the bump with `--skip-changelog` on an empty-`[Unreleased]` changelog and expects the file to stay byte-identical. With the guard gone, rotation would run and insert a heading, so I expect the test to fail. I didn't run it, so I've marked the outcome as unknown.\n\n{\"verdict\": \"violates\", \"decisions\": [\"ADR-0580\"], \"checks\": [\"advance: empty-[Unreleased] CHANGELOG.md byte-identical — no heading inserted, [Unreleased] ref unchanged\"], \"check_outcomes\": {\"advance: empty-[Unreleased] CHANGELOG.md byte-identical — no heading inserted, [Unreleased] ref unchanged\": \"unknown\"}}"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 934, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6088, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 934}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6f827a2c-b681-4fe7-a646-6bcccccc680c", "uuid": "227c120a-c075-429b-bf91-75d17a5e5fae", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:05:27.376Z", "request_id": "req_011ChSmhdTdSxcLAVSit8pfc"}}
